     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Ways of earning a living",
     "md": "People work to earn money. **Farmers** grow crops and keep animals. **Fishers** catch fish. **Traders** buy and sell goods. **Craftspeople** (tailors, carpenters, potters) make things. **Workers** in factories, offices, schools and hospitals give services. Farmers sell their crops, and the money buys what the family needs."
